{
"skill": "readability_scorer",
"input": "Briefly explain why a benchmark should include both easy and hard tasks."
},A benchmark should include both easy and hard tasks to provide a comprehensive assessment of a model's performance. Easy tasks are typically simple and straightforward, allowing the model to demonstrate its ability to perform well on basic, well-defined tasks. Hard tasks, on the other hand, are more complex and challenging, requiring the model to demonstrate its ability to generalize and perform well on more difficult tasks. By including both easy and hard tasks, a benchmark can evaluate a model's performance across a range of tasks and provide a more accurate assessment of its overall capabilities.

